Sales enablement. Build the pitch, the discovery questions, the objection handling, and the demo narrative. Sit in on calls and fix what is not landing.&nbsp;






Content that carries technical weight. Solution briefs, analyst submissions, webinars, launch blogs, and conference sessions on agentic AI assurance, LLM risk, and AI governance in CX.&nbsp;






Cross-functional partnership. Work daily with Product, Sales, Demand Gen, and Customer Success. Product marketing at Cyara is the connective tissue between what engineering builds and what a seller says on a call.&nbsp;



What we are looking for 

Required&nbsp;





5+ years in B2B SaaS or AI product marketing&nbsp;






A track record of shipping launches that moved pipeline, with the numbers to show it.&nbsp;






Writing and presentations that stands on its own. Concise, specific, no filler. We will ask for samples and we will read them closely.&nbsp;






Comfort with technical buyers and technical product teams.&nbsp;&nbsp;






Experience selling to enterprise accounts through a sales-led motion with long cycles and multiple stakeholders.&nbsp;




Bonus, and it counts for a lot&nbsp;




AI Native, Agentic AI startup experience&nbsp;






CX or contact center background —conversational AI, NLU, or contact center operations.&nbsp;






Experience in QA, testing, observability, or monitoring categories.&nbsp;




Why you should join us: &nbsp;Looking for a place where your ideas matter, your growth is accelerated, and your work creates real impact? Welcome to Cyara.&nbsp;&nbsp;We're building the assurance layer that gives enterprises the confidence to deploy agentic AI at scale with a global team that values curiosity, collaboration, and continuous learning. Whether you're launching new ideas, solving complex problems, or learning from talented colleagues across the world, you'll be surrounded by people who challenge and support you to do your best work.&nbsp;At Cyara, inclusivity isn't a buzzword, it's part of who we are. We foster a culture where everyone feels seen, heard, and empowered to contribute. Pair that with competitive pay, comprehensive benefits, flexible work options, recognition programs, and a strong focus on employee well-being, and you've got a workplace designed for both success and fulfilment.&nbsp;&nbsp;Big opportunities. Real impact. Amazing people. That's the Cyara experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;Cyara’s Diversity, Equity, Inclusive and Belonging Statement: &nbsp;At Cyara, we are dedicated to fostering a workplace that embodies equal opportunity and champions diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging (DEIB). We strive to cultivate an environment where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to bring their whole selves to work, contributing unique perspectives and talents. Our commitment includes continuously evaluating and enhancing our policies, practices, and culture to align with our DEIB principles. We ensure a discrimination-free environment where individuals are evaluated solely on their merits and abilities, regardless of legally protected statuses such as sex, race, color, ethnicity, national origin, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, or medical condition. By celebrating our differences and championing inclusivity, we enrich our organization, make more thoughtful decisions, and drive collective success. &nbsp;&nbsp;Cyara’s Values Statement: At Cyara, our values shape everything we do.&nbsp;We're&nbsp;passionate about Delivering Excellence by putting the customer first, collaborating globally, and always striving to improve.&nbsp;We take smart risks and Innovate Boldly,&nbsp;setting new standards and learning from every experience. Integrity First is our cornerstone,&nbsp;we value humility, authenticity, and respect for diversity, building trust in all we do.&nbsp;We Embrace Curiosity by empowering you to experiment, learn, and grow in a dynamic environment. At Cyara, our values drive us forward, shaping a culture where innovation and excellence thrive. &nbsp;&nbsp;Agencies:&nbsp;Thanks, but we’ve got this one!&nbsp; Please, no phone calls or emails to any employees of Cyara outside of the Talent Acquisition team.&nbsp; Cyara’s policy is to only accept resumes from Agencies via the Cyara Agency Portal. Agencies must have a valid fee agreement in&nbsp;place,&nbsp;and they must have been assigned the specific requisition to which they submit resumes, by the Cyara Talent Acquisition team before submitting any CVs. Any resume submitted outside of this process will be deemed the sole property of Cyara and, in the event, a candidate is submitted outside of this policy is hired, no fee or payment of any kind will be paid.Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type: &lt;/strong&gt;Full-time, salaried employment&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote in the UK only, with expected regular travel to retailer sites across the UK&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range: &lt;/strong&gt;£98,000 - £112,000&amp;nbsp;depending on experience + stock options&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Focal Systems is the industry leader in retail AI solutions. We are headquartered in San Francisco, California with operations in Canada and the UK, and a tech-hub in Poland. We are a Deep Learning first company. Our mission is to automate and optimize brick and mortar retail using deep learning computer vision. Focal Systems has been deployed at scale with some of the top retailers in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek smart, creative and passionate people who want to help build a great and enduring company and deploy Deep Learning to the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director of Operations, UK you will help build and lead the field operations team that installs and maintains Focal Systems shelf cameras across our UK retail partners. Our cameras are being deployed at scale, with 100,000+ units live or rolling out at leading retailers around the world, and the UK is a major part of that growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support the running of UK operations end to end: the people, the processes, the metrics, and the customer outcomes. You will work closely with senior and executive leadership to set and roll out operational strategy, and with Product, Engineering, and Customer Success to make every deployment faster, more reliable, and more cost-effective than the last.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be joining an established, experienced team that works in cycles. Retailer rollouts bring periods of rapid scale-up, followed by quieter maintenance periods where we scale back down, and those transitions have not always been smooth. A key part of this role is making them smoother: planning ahead for each change in pace, keeping the team steady and supported through it, and building processes that let us ramp up and down without losing quality or momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior leadership role. You will develop our existing team, support during scale-up and scale-down periods, set the operating rhythm for field work, and be the person our customers and colleagues rely on when something needs to get done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a hands-on operations leader who has scaled field teams and processes, and you are as comfortable working with stakeholders at different levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You run operations on data: you define the right metrics, watch them closely, and act early when they move&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build structure where there is none, designing roles, workflows, and SOPs that hold up as volume grows and priorities shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hire well, coach well, and build teams that take ownership without needing to be chased&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand that operations is a customer-facing function, and you take pride in exceeding what our retail partners expect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a fast-moving, remote-first environment and are energised by building something new&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own ongoing field-service performance and SLA delivery, prioritising maintenance work and driving issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and develop a high-performing UK field operations team responsible for installing and maintaining shelf cameras at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational plan for UK deployments, from scheduling and logistics through installation, quality checks, and ongoing maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, track, and report on the key metrics for field performance and SLA adherence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with executive leadership to set performance goals, budgets, and long-term operational strategy for the UK&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse operational processes end to end, identify bottlenecks, and lead improvements that increase speed, quality, and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across Product, Engineering, Supply Chain, and Customer Success to feed field insights back into hardware, software, and deployment playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior escalation point for operational and customer issues, removing blockers quickly and owning the outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with retail partners, understand their store operations, agree success criteria, and deliver against them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with any third-party installers or service partners, including performance, quality, and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish safe working practices and ensure field activity meets health and safety requirements at every retailer site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in an operations leadership role, with a track record of managing people, processes, and budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading field operations, installation, or service teams across multiple sites, ideally deploying hardware at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of core operational functions, including finance and budgeting, customer service, logistics, and people management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to plan and run operations for efficiency and productivity, using data and KPIs to drive decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and implementing new structures, roles, and processes that support rapid growth and shifting business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of account management and customer success, and comfort working directly with senior customer stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to present clearly to executives, customers, and field teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently in a remote environment and travel regularly within the UK&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of retail or grocery operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with retail technology such as shopper-facing apps, back-room inventory management, or POS systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing third-party installers, contractors, or service partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean Six Sigma or a similar process improvement certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth startup or scale-up environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Focal Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong Values and Mission - We are a tightly-knit team with an ambitious mission and a strong set of core values, which define our approach to business and have successfully guided us since inception.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exceptional Team - We are a team of hard-working, fun-loving professionals from some of the most eminent universities, research labs, and tech companies of our time. We pride ourselves on recruiting exceptional individuals to help us redefine the state-of-the-art.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Outstanding Partners - We work with 10+ of the largest retailers in the world and have a world-class roster of investors, advisors and partners to support &amp;amp; advise us in our endeavors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We care deeply about the health, happiness, and wellbeing of all of our employees. We offer:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Attractive Stock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sick Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development Budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Soho House, a &lt;strong&gt;Senior&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Chef de Partie &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW51313497 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW51313497 BCX0&quot;&gt;supports the kitchen brigade in delivering exceptional dining experiences to our members and guests. Y&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW245981133 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW245981133 BCX0&quot;&gt;ou will be instrumental in preparing, cooking, and presenting exceptional dishes in line with the club’s food philosophy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW245981133 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW12820748 BCX0&quot;&gt;Y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW12820748 BCX0&quot;&gt;our main responsibility is&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW66172363 BCX0&quot;&gt; to &lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW223324756 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW223324756 BCX0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW23000509 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW23000509 BCX0&quot;&gt;demonstrate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW23000509 BCX0&quot;&gt; technical &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW23000509 BCX0&quot;&gt;expertise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW23000509 BCX0&quot;&gt;, a strong understanding of kitchen operations, and a proactive attitude towards training, hygiene, and consistency. You will contribute to menu development, ensure compliance with allergy procedures and dietary requirements, and act as a role model to more junior kitchen staff.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW23000509 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW223324756 BCX0&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW223324756 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s in it for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly Pay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team meal whilst on shift prepared by our chefs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soho Friends Membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;50% Team discount on Food &amp;amp; Drink, 7 days a week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Staff Room Rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Cash Plan (option to up to 2 additional dependents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dental Plan (option to add up to 2 additional dependents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Birthday Day Off after 1 years&#39; continuous service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 50% Staff Discount on Cowshed &amp;amp; Soho Home&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In conjunction with Soho Impact, take 2 days paid a year to support a charity of your choice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Counselling Sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cookhouse &amp;amp; House Tonic: Our Cookhouse &amp;amp; Tonic Programmes offer unique food and drink training, events and opportunities to inspire and educate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous training to develop yourself personally and professionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Events: From fitness sessions to cinema screenings and art classes, each month we hold a series of fun events which you can sign up to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Soho House offers competitive compensation packages that feature global benefits and perks. Whether you’re seeking entry-level employment or a new opportunity to expand your profession, we offer training to develop the technical and managerial skills necessary to enhance your career&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key duties…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, cook, and present dishes within your section to the highest standards in quality, consistency, and presentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Sous Chef and Head Chef in delivering efficient and well-organized service during busy periods and events.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with all food safety, allergy, hygiene, and health standards, including HACCP and company policies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of mise en place and prep tasks, ensuring all elements are ready and of high quality for service.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the training and mentoring of Commis Chefs and Demi Chefs de Partie, helping to develop their technical skills and kitchen knowledge.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attending regular meetings with front and back of house teams to learn about any menu or service changes and specials alongside daily tastings. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in preparation of team meals as requested, considering dietary needs and variety.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate a proactive attitude towards learning, improvement, and teamwork.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting with the deep cleaning of the entire kitchen before close.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wrapping unused items and storing them in proper area at the end of service.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;A successful Senior Chef de Partie for Soho House will ideally have up to 2 years’ experience in a busy high-profile venue and a natural flair for first class service. You’ll be reliable, friendly and happy to be a key part of the team that strives for success. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2+ years’ experience in similar capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for food, attention to detail, and a strong desire to learn and grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of basic food safety and hygiene practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication and teamwork skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive, proactive, and respectful attitude in a busy kitchen environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culinary qualification (e.g., NVQ Level 1 or 2) is a plus but not essential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to demonstrate competency as outlined in the training schedule and Club School&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work flexible shifts and schedules, including weekends and holidays as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take direction, work in a team environment and autonomously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range for this role if filled within the UK is listed below. The range for the position in different geographies may vary based on market differences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£17.50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£17.50 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Affirm is reinventing credit to make it more honest and friendly, giving consumers the flexibility to buy now and pay later without any hidden fees or compounding interest.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re excited to welcome a new cohort of graduates with a computer science or related major who are ready to leverage their skills to drive real-world impact and shape the future of finance! &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In our hybrid early career program, you’ll be paired with a tenured Affirmer and have an opportunity to collaborate in-person 3 days a week out of our London office. You&#39;ll experience the best of both worlds: the in-office experience and remote work. After the one-year, you can remain hybrid, go remote, or stay in an office. Opportunities are available across different tech stacks and teams so that you can find a perfect fit to launch your career with Affirm!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;With the support of your team, you will work on tasks that contribute to the team&#39;s projects and goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;You will work collaboratively and proactively with your team and stakeholders, bringing them along for your work and helping to create visibility and dialog regarding the risks and trade-offs related to your work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;You will strike the right balance of speed and quality in your work, ensuring that we hit our business goals while protecting our systems from downtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;You will contribute to a sense of community on your team by engaging in growth and development activities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have mastered taking a simple problem or business scenario into a solution that interacts with multiple software components, and executing on it by writing clear, easily understood, well tested and extensible code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable navigating a large code base, debugging others&#39; code, and providing feedback to other engineers through code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your experience demonstrates that you take ownership of your growth, proactively seeking feedback from your team, your manager, and your stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong verbal and written communication skills that support effective collaboration with our global engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position requires either equivalent practical experience or a Bachelor’s degree in a related field.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-formula-id=&quot;_c_f_4zYZFddFQ5_0&quot; data-error=&quot;false&quot; data-placeholder=&quot;false&quot; data-loading=&quot;false&quot; data-recalculating=&quot;false&quot; data-inactive=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GBR base pay range per year: £&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-formula-id=&quot;_c_f_4zYZFddFQ5_0&quot; data-error=&quot;false&quot; data-placeholder=&quot;false&quot; data-loading=&quot;false&quot; data-recalculating=&quot;false&quot; data-inactive=&quot;false&quot;&gt;80,000&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;span data-formula-id=&quot;_c_f_4zYZFddFQ5_1&quot; data-error=&quot;false&quot; data-placeholder=&quot;false&quot; data-loading=&quot;false&quot; data-recalculating=&quot;false&quot; data-inactive=&quot;false&quot;&gt;118,000&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location (Hybrid): London&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By clicking &quot;Submit Application,&quot; you acknowledge that you have read Affirm&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.affirm.com/global-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and consent to the use of your personal information as described.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Twilio, we’re shaping the future of communications, all from the comfort of our homes. We deliver innovative solutions to&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;hundreds of thousands of businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and empower millions of developers worldwide to craft personalized customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our dedication to &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;remote-first work&lt;/a&gt;, and strong culture of connection and global inclusion means that no matter your location, you’re part of a vibrant team with diverse experiences making a global impact each day. As we continue to revolutionize how the world interacts, we’re acquiring new skills and experiences that make work feel truly rewarding. Your career at Twilio is in your hands.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring and how we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next Strategic Account Executive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to sell into high value prospects and customers. This person will play a key role in further growing the business across EMEA with a particular focus on Southern Europe. The candidate will be responsible for managing fast growing customers in the region. Focused mainly on Product cross and up-sell and GP growth, as well as sourcing net new opportunities within a set of accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Servicing the fastest growing customers in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing our revenue and gross profit share of wallet within your key account list.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opening doors to the purchase of Twilio’s products and services - including voice, messaging, email, contact centre, account security software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining the highest levels of customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create pricing proposals, negotiating terms and managing the contract process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Selling solutions to a technical and business audience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building trust and mutual respect with technical customers and peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thinking outside of the box and having extraordinary interpersonal and communication skills to make complex contractual, technical, and financial details sound simple.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balancing challenging priorities and handling multiple projects/deals at the same time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native or bilingual proficiency in both English and Hebrew&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of Account Management/Sales experience covering selling and closing complex technical solutions to a large customer base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of working with accounts ranging from large multinational enterprise customers to SMB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success by achieving quota on a consistent basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of Account Management experience and a solid understanding of how to cross sell and upsell solutions within a mature customer base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid understanding of financial reporting within a direct customer base - Revenue and Gross Profit tracking, Risk and Opportunity (net new business) cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally, you also have experience selling both to a business and technical audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and understanding of working in the communications market is preferable.&amp;nbsp; Have sold or worked with Messaging, Voice Calling, Email, Account Security Verification.&amp;nbsp; Or have prior experience in a traditional telecommunications environment/business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position will be based in the United Kingdom, Spain or Ireland&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportunities to build relationships with our customers and each other. For this role, approximately 25%&amp;nbsp; travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Twilio offers many benefits, including competitive pay, generous time off, ample parental and wellness leave, healthcare, a retirement savings program, and much more. Offerings vary by location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio thinks big. Do you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We like to solve problems, take initiative, pitch in when needed, and are always up for trying new things. That&#39;s why we seek out colleagues who embody our values — something we call &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/values&quot;&gt;Twilio Magic&lt;/a&gt;. Additionally, we empower employees to build &lt;a href=&quot;https://twilio.org/support-and-resources/impact-fund&quot;&gt;positive change in their communities&lt;/a&gt; by supporting their volunteering and donation efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, if you&#39;re ready to unleash your full potential, do your best work, and be the best version of yourself, apply now! If this role isn&#39;t what you&#39;re looking for, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/jobs#open-positions&quot;&gt;please consider other open positions.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay alert to recruitment fraud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care about your safety. Scammers sometimes impersonate Twilio recruiters through fake job postings, emails, websites, or messages. Please ensure you are engaging with an official @&lt;a href=&quot;http://twilio.com&quot;&gt;twilio.com&lt;/a&gt; email address. We will never ask for payment, gift cards, cryptocurrency, or banking information during the recruiting process. We do not make job offers without a formal interview process or conduct interviews exclusively through text-based messaging apps.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio is proud to be an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/strong&gt; We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment in accordance with the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers and the California Fair Chance Act. Additionally, Twilio participates in the E-Verify program in certain locations, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;Join New Era Technology, where People First is at the heart of everything we do. With a global team of over 3,000 professionals, we&#39;re committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels valued, empowered, and inspired to grow. Our mission is to securely connect people, places, and information with end-to-end technology solutions at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;At New Era, you&#39;ll join a team-oriented culture that prioritizes your personal and professional development. Work alongside industry-certified experts, access continuous training, and enjoy competitive benefits. Guided by our core attributes — putting people first, embracing continuous learning, and thriving through collaboration and inclusion — we nurture our people to deliver exceptional customer service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;If you want to make an impact in a supportive, growth-oriented environment, New Era is the place for you. Apply today and help us shape the future of work—together&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Human Resources Director, Europe &amp;amp; Canada&lt;/strong&gt; is responsible for leading the HR strategy, operations, and employee experience across Canada, the United Kingdom, Belgium, and Romania. This position serves as the senior HR leader for the region and partners closely with business leaders to align people strategies with organizational priorities, business growth, and operational objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the Chief Human Resources Officer in the United States, the HR Director will provide leadership across employee relations, talent acquisition, organizational design, workforce planning, talent and leadership development, succession planning, payroll oversight, employment compliance, and general HR operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will bring strong experience operating in a complex, multi-country environment and will balance strategic leadership with effective day-to-day HR execution. The role will lead regional HR resources while collaborating closely with global HR, Talent Acquisition, Payroll, Finance, Legal, and business leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Human Resources Director, Europe &amp;amp; Canada will have 3 direct reports and serves approximately 250 employees in the region.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIMARY DUTIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic HR Leadership &amp;amp; Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the senior HR leader for Canada, the UK, Belgium, and Romania, providing strategic HR direction across the region. Other countries with small numbers of staff include France, Ireland, and the Netherlands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with EOR vendors for employment needs in countries outside of the company’s operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders and managers to translate business priorities into people strategies that drive growth, engagement, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use workforce data and insights to identify trends, risks, and opportunities, and adapt global HR initiatives to country-specific needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Operations &amp;amp; Regional Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional HR operations, ensuring consistent, scalable, and employee-focused HR practices across the employee lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the regional HR team, including HR Managers in the UK and Romania and an HR Coordinator in Romania.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global HR to standardize and continuously improve processes while addressing local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Relations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead employee relations matters across the region, including disciplinary actions, grievances, investigations, redundancies, and dismissals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach managers to address employee relations and performance issues consistently, with appropriate documentation and escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with General Counsel and external counsel on employment-related claims and proactively reduce employment risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Acquisition &amp;amp; Onboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional recruitment and onboarding of top talent in partnership with offshore recruiters and hiring managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build talent pipelines for critical roles and ensure hiring practices and documentation meet local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Development, Succession &amp;amp; Career Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead employee development, succession planning, career pathing, and leadership development across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate talent reviews with leaders to identify critical roles, high-potential employees, and capability gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll &amp;amp; HR Administration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee regional payroll administration in partnership with the offshore payroll specialist team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong controls and coordination between HR, Payroll, and Finance for accurate employee transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Compliance &amp;amp; Risk Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure HR practices comply with employment requirements in Canada, the UK, Belgium, and Romania.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor legislative developments and recommend updates to policies, documentation, and manager practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance for working time, leave, employee consultation, restructurings, redundancies, and terminations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organizational Effectiveness &amp;amp; Workforce Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance on organizational structure, spans of control, and workforce planning to support growth and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integrations, restructurings, acquisitions, and related change and communication strategies within the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPERIENCE REQUIRED:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant progressive HR leadership experience, including experience at the HR Director, Head of HR, Senior HR Business Partner, or comparable level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience supporting employees and leaders across multiple countries or jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of employment practices and employee relations within the UK and broader European environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing complex employee relations matters, including investigations, disciplinary matters, grievances, redundancies, and dismissals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with senior business leaders on workforce planning, organizational design, restructuring, and talent strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing HR professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of recruitment, onboarding, performance management, succession planning and employee development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing oversight or governance for payroll and HR operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and demonstrated ability to handle confidential and sensitive employee matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, influencing, consultation, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively within a global organization and collaborate across countries, cultures, and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct HR experience supporting employees in Canada, the United Kingdom, Belgium, and/or Romania.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a global professional services, technology services, managed services, or similarly complex organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting acquisitions, integrations, restructurings, or other large-scale organizational transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within a global HR operating model that uses shared-services or offshore recruiting, payroll, or HR operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEADERSHIP COMPETENCIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Business Partnership: &lt;/strong&gt;Connects workforce and organizational decisions directly to business priorities and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Acumen: &lt;/strong&gt;Understands how talent, organizational structure, workforce costs, and leadership capability affect business performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Risk Judgment: &lt;/strong&gt;Balances employee experience, business objectives, consistency, and employment risk when advising leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence &amp;amp; Credibility: &lt;/strong&gt;Builds trusted relationships with senior executives, managers, employees, and global functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Effectively leads organizations and employees through transformation, restructuring, integration, and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Proactively develops internal talent and strengthens leadership pipelines and succession plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence: &lt;/strong&gt;Creates consistent, scalable HR processes while recognizing when local requirements require different approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global &amp;amp; Cultural Awareness: &lt;/strong&gt;Works effectively across countries and cultures and avoids applying a single-country approach to regional workforce matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sound Judgment &amp;amp; Discretion: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrates maturity and confidentiality when handling sensitive employee and legal matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LANGUAGE SKILLS: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to read, understand, and interpret job-related documents, instructions, policies, and communications in English. Ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing, with employees, customers, vendors, and other business partners, as applicable to the position. Fluent English is required. Fluent or professional-level French language capability is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED EDUCATION / CERTIFICATIONS: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Human Resources, Business, Organizational Development, or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant professional experience. Preferred: CIPD or an equivalent internationally recognized HR credential.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHYSICAL DEMANDS:&lt;/strong&gt; Regular use of hands and fingers to operate a computer, keyboard, mouse, and other office equipment, including repetitive motions such as typing, scrolling, and mouse use. Ability to communicate effectively and understand verbal communication in person, by telephone, and through video conferencing or other remote communication tools. Ability to view and read information on computer screens and printed materials, including the ability to adjust focus. The position requires prolonged periods of computer use and viewing a computer screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WORK ENVIRONMENT: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPECTED HOURS OF WORK: &lt;/strong&gt;This position generally operates during normal business hours; however, specific start and end times may vary based on business needs, workload, and job responsibilities. Occasional work outside of normal business hours may be required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRAVEL: &lt;/strong&gt;Occasional trips to Belgium and Romania may be required.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SALARY:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; This role will have 3 direct reports and serve approximately 250 people in the region.&amp;nbsp; Salary is $75,000 £ - $85,000 £&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;New Era Technology, LLC., and its subsidiaries (“New Era” “we”, “us”, or “our”) in its operating regions worldwide are committed to respecting your privacy and recognize the need for appropriate protection and management of any Personal Data that you may provide us. In this, we are also committed to providing you with a positive experience on our websites and while using our products, services and solutions (“Solutions”).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;View our Privacy Policy here &lt;a id=&quot;menur1e55&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;https://www.neweratech.com/us/privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;menur1e57&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;https://www.neweratech.com/us/privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.neweratech.com/us/privacy-policy/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;We never ask candidates to pay any fees at any point in our hiring process. If you are ever asked to provide payment for training, certification, equipment, or any other purpose, it is not from our company. Only communications from our official company channels should be trusted. Please note our official email domain is ----- If you suspect fraudulent activity, please contact us immediately at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- .&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Threecolts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Threecolts is a software suite built for consumer brands, helping them recover revenue, operate more efficiently and grow across major retailers and marketplaces.&lt;br&gt;Our largest business, Margin Pro, helps brands recover money owed to them by retailers and marketplaces such as Amazon, Walmart and Target by managing disputes on their behalf. Alongside this, we’re building and scaling newer products, including AI Operator and Retail 365, while continuing to grow our portfolio of subscription products across our customer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a global team of 340 people across 33 teams, having grown through 24 acquisitions. We operate with a flat structure, giving people real ownership and the ability to move quickly. AI is embedded in how we work across the business, helping us increase speed, improve quality and operate at scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔥 Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll take ownership of features across Inventory Lab’s C# and .NET-based systems, delivering them from initial design through to production. You’ll design, develop, and maintain clean, scalable backend services, APIs, and application components using C# and the .NET ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with modern .NET technologies, including ASP.NET and ASP.NET Core, to build and maintain reliable, high-performance web applications and services. You’ll focus on writing maintainable, well-tested code that supports the product’s evolving requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll develop and maintain front-end features using Vue.js and TypeScript, building responsive, intuitive, and maintainable user interfaces that integrate seamlessly with backend APIs. You’ll take ownership of full-stack features end to end, from designing backend services and data models to implementing front-end components, managing application state, and ensuring a consistent user experience. You’ll collaborate with Product, QA, and DevOps to deliver reliable, performant features across the entire application stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate independently within a defined scope, making sound technical decisions and balancing delivery speed with long-term quality. You’ll actively improve existing systems, debug production issues, identify root causes, and implement durable fixes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll contribute to technical discussions, help evolve architecture within your domain, and raise engineering standards through thoughtful code reviews. Collaboration is key: you’ll work closely with Product, QA, and DevOps to deliver features and improvements that provide meaningful value to Inventory Lab customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;😊 About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–8+ years of professional software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;C#&lt;/strong&gt; and experience building production-grade applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the &lt;strong&gt;.NET platform&lt;/strong&gt;, including its runtime, libraries, and application development ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing web applications and backend services using &lt;strong&gt;ASP.NET and ASP.NET Core&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing modern web applications using Vue.js or React, including component-based architecture and reusable components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building responsive, accessible user interfaces and integrating front-end applications with REST APIs, and maintaining backend services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of system design, application architecture, and scalable software development patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with SQL databases, relational data models, and query optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud infrastructure: AWS or Azure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging production systems, investigating root causes, and resolving issues independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with Git, code reviews, automated testing, and collaborative development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively within an existing codebase and improve code quality without over-engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💼 What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have a strong ownership mindset and consistently deliver high-quality work. You make pragmatic technical decisions, understanding when to prioritize speed and when to invest in scalability, reliability, and maintainability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You understand the practical application of C# and the .NET ecosystem, choosing appropriate frameworks and patterns to build reliable software. You’re comfortable working with existing systems, identifying opportunities for improvement, and delivering solutions that balance immediate business needs with long-term technical quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You thrive in a product-led environment and care about the customer impact of what you build. You communicate clearly, collaborate effectively across teams, and look for ways to improve both the product and engineering processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll support Inventory Lab, a product used by e-commerce sellers to manage inventory, listings, accounting, and operational workflows. The work will suit someone who enjoys solving practical product problems, improving system reliability, and building software that supports real customer use cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⛳️ Compensation, Perks &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Salary: £ 110,000 per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;25 days PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Healthcare &amp;amp; Pension benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Opportunity to join company-wide offsites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Regular rate reviews and bonus opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Fully remote/hybrid working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Description:&lt;/strong&gt; Systemiq is a system-change company committed to achieving the Sustainable Development Goals and the Paris Agreement by transforming markets and business models across five key systems: nature and food, materials and circularity, energy, urban areas, and sustainable finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a certified B Corp, we combine strategic advisory with high-impact, on-the-ground work, partnering with business, finance, policymakers and civil society to deliver system change. With offices across Africa, Asia, Europe and the Americas, we are dedicated exclusively to sustainability-focused work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strategy Associate, Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: London preferred. Amsterdam also possible&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Systemiq is looking for a Strategy Associate to join our Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy team. This role is suited to someone who combines strong strategic thinking with the intellectual curiosity to tackle complex sustainability challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on some of the most important questions facing companies, governments and wider society as they shift towards more circular and sustainable models. Projects can range from shaping corporate strategy and identifying new business opportunities to assessing value chains, developing policy recommendations and designing system-level interventions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can bring the core toolkit and pace of a strong strategy consultant: structured problem-solving, analytical rigour, clear communication and sound judgement. Strategy consulting experience is one route to demonstrating this. We are equally interested in candidates from other demanding analytical environments who can show the same quality of thinking and ability to turn complexity into clear recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join small, senior-led project teams and take meaningful responsibility from the outset. You will structure problems, conduct analysis, develop insights and work directly with clients to translate those insights into practical strategic choices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structure complex problems:&lt;/strong&gt; break ambiguous questions into clear workstreams, hypotheses and analytical priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate insights:&lt;/strong&gt; conduct rigorous qualitative and quantitative analysis, drawing conclusions from incomplete or complex information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape recommendations:&lt;/strong&gt; translate analysis into clear, concise and practical strategic recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop client materials:&lt;/strong&gt; produce high-quality presentations, briefings and other client-ready outputs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with clients:&lt;/strong&gt; work directly with senior stakeholders across businesses, governments, foundations and non-governmental organisations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to project direction:&lt;/strong&gt; help shape project approaches, hypotheses and emerging strategic conclusions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build trusted relationships:&lt;/strong&gt; work effectively with clients, partners and stakeholders across multi-organisation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be part of Systemiq&#39;s Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy platform, led by Partner Ben Dixon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ben works across circular economy and energy topics and has advised organisations including the Ellen MacArthur Foundation, the United Nations International Resource Panel and multinational companies across packaging, chemicals and related sectors. He also leads Systemiq&#39;s work on plastics, focused on accelerating the transition towards a more circular and resource-efficient plastics system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Strategy and analytical capability&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for candidates who already demonstrate, or can quickly operate with, the core toolkit expected in strategy consulting. You should be able to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Structure complex and ambiguous problems into clear components, hypotheses and analytical questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply strong analytical judgement to qualitative and quantitative information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Synthesize complex material into concise insights and decision-relevant recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicate clearly in writing and verbally, including through high-quality presentation materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work effectively at pace, managing changing priorities and imperfect information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Move comfortably between detailed analysis and the broader strategic question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience and background&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will typically bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least two years of experience in strategy consulting, advisory or another analytically demanding environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evidence of strong performance and increasing responsibility in your previous roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience contributing to strategy, investment, commercial or other decision-focused work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong academic achievement, typically including a Master&#39;s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We particularly welcome candidates from strategy consulting, but relevant experience could also come from corporate strategy, investing, high-growth businesses, specialist advisory firms or other project-based environments where structured thinking and analytical rigour are central to the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Sector interest and understanding&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be a specialist across every part of the Materials &amp;amp; Circular Economy agenda. You should, however, bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An understanding of, or demonstrated ability to learn, complex industrial and consumer value chains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exposure to sectors such as plastics, petrochemicals, chemicals, consumer goods, manufacturing, mobility, energy or waste management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong interest in sustainability, circular economy and the economic and strategic questions involved in system change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Location&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London is the preferred location for this role. We would also consider Amsterdam for candidates whose experience and capabilities are an especially strong match for the position.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;description__body&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;578&quot; data-end=&quot;603&quot;&gt;Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br data-start=&quot;603&quot; data-end=&quot;606&quot;&gt;At Systemiq, we absolutely believe diverse perspectives are essential to driving system change. We are committed to creating an inclusive workplace where people feel respected, supported and able to do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.systemiq.earth/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to view our Data Policy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(40, 40, 40);&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Our leading SaaS-based Global Employment Platform™ enables clients to expand into over 180 countries quickly and efficiently, without the complexities of establishing local entities. At G-P, we’re dedicated to breaking down barriers to global business and creating opportunities for everyone, everywhere.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Our diverse, remote-first teams are essential to our success. We empower our Dream Team members with flexibility and resources, fostering an environment where innovation thrives and every contribution is valued and celebrated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The work you do here will positively impact lives around the world. We stand by our promise: Opportunity Made Possible. In addition to competitive compensation and benefits, we invite you to join us in expanding your skills and helping to reshape the future of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;At G-P, we assist organizations in building exceptional global teams in days, not months—streamlining the hiring, onboarding, and management process to unlock growth potential for all.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;As the Sr. Director &amp;amp; Head of Architecture at G-P, you will be the visionary leader responsible for defining and executing the long-term technical strategy for our global products and AI platforms and influence technical decisions across the company. This is a high-impact, executive-level role that bridges the gap between complex engineering execution and high-level business objectives. You will oversee the evolution of our cloud-native ecosystem, ensuring our architecture is scalable, secure, and infused with cutting-edge AI/ML capabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Reporting directly to the Head of Engineering, you will lead a high-performing team of Architects. You will work in close lockstep with Product Management, Engineering to harmonize technology decisions across the organization, ensuring our investment in technology translates directly into market-leading customer experiences&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Strategic Technical Leadership: Define and strongly influence the execution of a target-state, AI-native architecture that supports both core software services and advanced AI Agentic behaviors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Architectural Governance: Establish global standards for architecture consistency, ensuring all platform components maximize reuse and align with the long-term technology roadmap.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;AI First thinking: Oversee the architectural design of complex AI systems, AI enablement strategies, data engineering, and governance controls. Ensure that these are integrated into a cohesive strategy and implementation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Customer Centricity: Everything we do is to serve our customers. Understanding the customers and the business is the only way to build strategies for it’s success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Team Management &amp;amp; Mentorship: Lead, scale, and mentor a multidisciplinary team of architects, fostering a culture of engineering excellence and continuous learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Security &amp;amp; Compliance: Define and create standards and governance mechanisms for software platform and infrastructure security to mitigate data breaches and ensure regulatory compliance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Technical Trade-offs: Act as a coach and decision maker with technical teams and business stakeholders, translating complex technical trade-offs when creating business impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Innovation &amp;amp; Research: Serve as the ultimate &quot;sounding board&quot; for introducing new technologies, 3rd-party integrations, and open-source solutions to keep the platform at the forefront of the industry.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Reliability &amp;amp; Performance: Ensure system and infrastructure architecture results in high reliability, low latency, and minimal outages as a primary measure of organizational success.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Culture Builder: Help create a strong culture of innovation and technical excellence across the organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;15+ years of experience in software engineering and architecture, building products and platforms with at least 5 years in a senior leadership or directorial capacity managing Architecture teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Extensive Cloud Expertise: Proven track record of designing and deploying distributed, cloud-native architectures, especially AWS.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;AI First Product &amp;amp; Tech Strategies : Experience&amp;nbsp; with building AI Native products and technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Strategic Communication: Demonstrated ability to gain buy-in for large-scale technical shifts from both executive leadership and hands-on engineering teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Change Management: Experience leading architectural digital transformations within a rapidly growing or &quot;unstructured&quot; corporate environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Financial Acumen: Ability to analyze technology trade-offs through the lens of Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) and ROI.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Education: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;message-list_1761669766.039629&quot; class=&quot;c-virtual_list__item&quot; data-qa=&quot;virtual-list-item&quot; data-item-key=&quot;1761669766.039629&quot;&gt;
