&lt;p&gt;CreateFuture is an AI-native consulting partner where people do work that matters and are supported to do it well. We work side by side with our clients, challenging what&#39;s not working and helping them to build the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work alongside organisations such as PayPal, adidas, NatWest, FanDuel, and Money Saving Expert, building digital products and services that make a difference while always putting people first. Our commitment to craft, quality, and culture has helped us scale to over 600 people in just a few years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role and team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our .Net engineering capability builds backend services and APIs for clients across sectors, from payment integrations to large-scale platform migrations, always working as part of cross-functional scrum teams alongside testers, product owners and designers. As a Senior .Net Engineer, you&#39;ll take ownership of complex backend components end-to-end, operating with greater autonomy while mentoring less experienced colleagues. You&#39;ll be a trusted technical voice within your project team, helping to shape how the team builds, tests and ships software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and building backend services and APIs in C# and .NET/.NET Core, taking ownership of technical decisions within your area with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating with third-party APIs and systems, such as payment gateways, and designing resilient, well-documented interfaces for other developers to consume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring and supporting less experienced engineers through code review, pairing and technical guidance, helping them grow their skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Championing engineering best practice, clean code, and thorough unit and integration testing across your project team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working as a senior member of a cross-functional scrum team, contributing to technical decisions, estimation and planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying opportunities to improve the scalability, maintainability and long-term robustness of the codebase, and proposing solutions to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to talk to you if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong, proven experience building APIs using C# and .NET/.NET Core, including ORM and dependency injection experience with relational or NoSQL data stores such as SQL Server, PostgreSQL or Cosmos DB, at a senior level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of mentoring or supporting less experienced engineers, through code review, pairing or technical coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have deep experience with engineering best practice, clean code and a strong testing culture, including unit and integration testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working as part of a cross-functional development team using Agile practices; experience with other languages and frameworks such as JavaScript/Node.js, Java/Spring, TypeScript, Scala, Kotlin or Python is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have cloud experience using AWS or Azure (Azure is especially common on .NET stacks) — the specific provider matters less than solid cloud fundamentals; experience with infrastructure-as-code tooling such as Terraform, Bicep or ARM Templates is a plus, and we&#39;re happy to help you broaden your platform knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
